WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.130 --> 00:00:01.722
- Well let's talk about some favorites.

00:00:01.722 --> 00:00:04.500
So what inspired "The Dance?"

00:00:04.500 --> 00:00:06.090
- I was sittin' at The Bluebird,

00:00:06.090 --> 00:00:07.600
there was probably about
seven or eight of us,

00:00:07.600 --> 00:00:08.900
there was this guy named Tony Arata

00:00:08.900 --> 00:00:12.710
was sittin' there playin' and
Tony starts in on this song

00:00:12.710 --> 00:00:15.400
and when he gets done
with it I'm just amazed

00:00:15.400 --> 00:00:16.460
and nobody in the room

00:00:16.460 --> 00:00:20.170
seems to be gettin' the same
reaction that I'm getting.

00:00:20.170 --> 00:00:21.770
And so I take it to Allen Reynolds,

00:00:21.770 --> 00:00:24.870
Allen Reynolds says he
loves it and we keep waitin'

00:00:24.870 --> 00:00:26.327
and keep waitin' and
finally Allen Reynolds goes,

00:00:26.327 --> 00:00:27.730
"How come we haven't cut "The Dance" yet?

00:00:27.730 --> 00:00:29.380
'Cause the album was almost over.

00:00:29.380 --> 00:00:32.070
I said, "I'm not sure
that it's country enough."

00:00:32.070 --> 00:00:32.903
- What?

00:00:32.903 --> 00:00:35.120
- You know, 'cause this
bein' from Oklahoma

00:00:35.120 --> 00:00:37.007
and it had piano in it, which you know,

00:00:37.007 --> 00:00:39.170
I had moved to Nashville,
didn't know what a piano was,

00:00:39.170 --> 00:00:40.570
'cause it's always just
steels and fiddles.

00:00:40.570 --> 00:00:42.900
- Yes but your voice is country music.

00:00:42.900 --> 00:00:43.980
- Thank you.
- You tie it in.

00:00:43.980 --> 00:00:45.810
- It's funny, 'cause that's what he said.

00:00:45.810 --> 00:00:46.643
And he told me, he said,

00:00:46.643 --> 00:00:47.960
"Pal, I'm gonna tell you right now,"

00:00:47.960 --> 00:00:50.007
he always used the word pal, he says,

00:00:50.007 --> 00:00:51.920
"If you don't cut 'The Dance',

00:00:51.920 --> 00:00:53.440
if you don't record that song,

00:00:53.440 --> 00:00:55.790
it'll be the biggest hit you never had.

00:00:55.790 --> 00:00:57.230
- Oh wow.

00:00:57.230 --> 00:00:59.950
- It's cool.
- Challenge accepted.

00:00:59.950 --> 00:01:04.527
- Yeah, it's just,
what's the, oh thank you.

00:01:05.761 --> 00:01:09.670
♪ Lookin' back on the- ♪

00:01:09.670 --> 00:01:10.645
- Quit, don't do that!

00:01:10.645 --> 00:01:13.266
- I have to do it!
(Garth laughs)

00:01:13.266 --> 00:01:17.317
I am literally, like I
can't believe my life!

00:01:17.317 --> 00:01:18.150
(Garth laughing)

00:01:18.150 --> 00:01:21.550
Like, April, Beck and Mary McConnell,

00:01:21.550 --> 00:01:24.047
all my friends from
childhood hate me right now!

00:01:25.120 --> 00:01:26.540
I'm so sorry April.

00:01:26.540 --> 00:01:28.150
She's the one that introduced you to me!

00:01:28.150 --> 00:01:31.053
And I like, I feel like
I'm stealing her moment.

